From 06abdfa50aef6e5068869bc7552fafa5e99b7b9d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cass <867000+Cass67@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 05:10:10 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] pipeline-windows: overlap three or more layer-split stages;
 HIP drafter scratch race

--pipeline-windows 2 now runs on any layer split with two or more stages. Every
stage but the last is a front stage: the guessed window follows the verified
one through them one card behind (an odd verifier and an odd hand-off on every
boundary, a pair of GDN snapshots on every front stage, commits and the undo
per stage), and only the last stage waits for the verdict. The pipelined prompt
read (--pipeline-windows 1) and --adapt-async stay two-stage.

HIP: the draft layer's per-row gr_read used the last stage's session scratch
(ss.block.gr), which that stage's verifier also uses in lm_head_mix. A chain
launched at a verdict and the next window's last stage can run on the card at
once after a guess that held, and the window's head then read a clobbered mix.
The draft layer now carves its own GrWorkspace.

Measured on 4x RX 7900 XT (Flash-Next GSQ-RCO IQ3_S, split 12,24,36, every
expert in VRAM, greedy, reasoning off): decode 59.4 -> 67.6 tok/s at 4K and
51.8 -> 65.6 at 32K. Greedy text identical to the serial loop on four prompts
with STRATA_IQ_MT_MIN=1 --pcie-frac 0 --adapt-every 0, also with every guess
forced wrong. Debug knob STRATA_PIPELINE_SPEC_DEPTH. Two-stage path not re-run
on two cards.
